Z||000000||Fierodave2001||04-11-2001||10:53 PM||||Hi, Dave here         ***updated 4-11-2001***<P>Hello to all those that I met at the show.<P>The Daytona show was just great. Many really<BR>nice Fiero's of every type were there. <P>I think the Fiero owners were the nicest and most happy to be around. Follow this path for<BR>my pic's.  (I've added more to the album)<BR> <A HREF="http://www.zing.com/album/pictures.html?id=4292795563" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zing.com/album/pictures.html?id=4292795563</A> <P>I still can not believe it. There were so many really sharp cars in the show. I'm just so proud to have my car selected.<P>I own the blue stock 87 GT that won the best Stock Paint, Best of Stock Group, and Best of Show. It has only 1730 miles !<P>I've owned the car since Sept 86, when I ordered it. I earlier owned a 84 4cyl coupe, then traded in for an 85 V6 SE. Just loved<BR>the heck out of each. When I bought the 87, I knew with the first look, it was a keeper.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1award.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by Fierodave2001 (edited 04-13-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Phil||04-11-2001||11:01 PM||||You gotta drive that thing more.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierodave2001||04-11-2001||11:34 PM||||Now that I know how to drive a trailer, no problem !!  Now, I'll drive it anywhere !!<BR>(off & on the Trailer !)  8-)<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||tgowens||04-12-2001||12:07 AM||||better be careful though, some of the rules may change at some of the shows and the trailered vehicles will be in a class all of their own..........at least it's been discussed a time or two.<P>I do have to admit though, that is one beautiful car and well deserving of the trophies it won at Daytona!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierodave2001||04-12-2001||12:23 AM||||Thanks for the good words.  I did not expect to win anything. I thought the Red 88 GT was going to win best paint.  I was told because he buffed out the paint, that made mine more stock.<P>I'm wondering about the Carlisle PA show.  I'm not sure if would be liked as well.  I was just floored that it did so well in Daytona.  <P>Think it would do good there ?  I was told the PA show is one of the largest in the northeast.||||reg||1
Z||000005||RossT||04-12-2001||12:47 AM||||I have to agree that the blue 87gt is my favorite color.<P>Dave, congrads on your win!!  But don't be afraid to drive it (a little)!  <P>My first fiero was an 88gt sunroof car that I bought May/1999.  It only had 400 miles on it!  I then found in May/2000 a 88gt t-top car with 940 miles on it!  I sold the sunroof car (now with 800 miles on it) and bought the t-top car!! I plan on about 500 miles a year on it!  You have to enjoy what you have.  It drove me nuts all winter to see my car in the corner of the garage, just waiting for spring!!!<P>BTW if you ever want to sell, post here first!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierodave2001||04-12-2001||11:44 AM||||Thanks for the good words.  What color is<BR>yours ?<P>||||reg||1
